 "catalogCode": "*16A07U",
 "notes": [
  "M.E.T. General Guidelines\nGeneral Guidelines\n- A minimum of 38 upper division business units is required.\n- Students must complete the degree program in eight semesters, not including Summer Session.\n- Students must complete ALL of their business prerequisite courses (including R&C) by the spring semester of their sophomore (2nd) year. Required prerequisite courses are: UGBA 10X; ECON 1 or ECON 2; Math 51 & Math 52 , or Math 53 or Math 54; Reading & Composition Parts A & B; and, depending on their major track, students may choose one of the following statistics courses or combinations:\n- EECS 126\n- ENGIN 178 (recommended for ME)\n- INDENG 172 (required for IEOR)\n- STAT 20\n- STAT 21/STAT W21\n- STAT C131A\n- STAT 134 (recommended for BioE)\n- STAT/DATA C140\n- DATA C8, plus:\n- UGBA 88, or\n- CIV ENG 93, or\n- DATA 89, or\n- DATA C88S/STAT C88S\n- DATA C100, plus:\n- UGBA 88, or\n- CIV ENG 93, or\n- DATA 89, or\n- DATA C88S/STAT 88S\n- All Haas business courses must be taken for a letter grade, including core substitutions, with the exception of UGBA 194, UGBA 198 and UGBA 199 (only offered Pass/No Pass).\n- Students who receive a grade of D+ or lower in a core UGBA course must repeat the course until they achieve a grade of C- or better.\n- All technical courses that can be used to fulfill a requirement must be taken for a letter grade.\n- Two M.E.T. Special Topics courses are required. One during the first year, first semester and another during the third year, first semester. M.E.T. Special Topics courses will count as upper division business elective units. A passing grade of C- or better is required.\n- Students in this program must adhere to all policies and procedures of the College of Engineering and the Haas School of Business.\n- Students must complete the College Requirements and the Program Major Requirements."
